# Copy to `.env` and edit. Nothing here is required to run the app: with an
# empty file it boots fully public, reports nothing to the hub, and serves
# every documentation page. Each block below says what turns ON when you set
# it, and what the app does when you don't.
#
# `.env` is gitignored and excluded from the Docker image (.dockerignore) —
# never bake a developer's copy into a production build. On Render, set these
# in the dashboard rather than committing a file; render.yaml documents the
# production values.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# flask | fastapi | quart. FastAPI is the local default (run.py); the Docker
# image pins flask because gunicorn serves WSGI. See lib/backend.py.
# DASH_BACKEND=fastapi

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public origin (lib/constants.py)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Drives <link rel="canonical">, sitemap.xml and the absolute URLs in
# llms.txt. Both names are honoured, one value — APP_BASE_URL (the
# network-wide spelling) wins. In production (RENDER set, or
# APP_ENV=production) the boot REFUSES unless one of them is set:
# see require_owned_base_url() in lib/constants.py.
# APP_BASE_URL=https://emojimart.2plot.dev
# DASH_EMOJI_MART_BASE_URL=https://emojimart.2plot.dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2plot network analytics (lib/satellite_reporter.py, lib/traffic_rollup.py)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The shared HMAC secret every satellite holds (same value as on 2plot.ai).
# Without it the app serves normally and reports nothing.
# CROSS_APP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# The series this app reports under — its key in the hub's network directory.
# SATELLITE_APP_KEY=emojimart
# The visitor ledger traffic_rollup reads. Production points this at the
# mounted disk (see render.yaml); locally the repo-root default is fine.
# TRAFFIC_ANALYTICS_FILE=/var/data/visitor_analytics.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Corpus document tiers (lib/page_tiers.py; registered in run.py)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Access tier for the tiered corpus documents served by dash-improve-my-llms
# >= 2.4.0: /llms-small.txt (compact briefing) and /llms-full.txt (every
# page's prose in one fetch). Values: public | auth | admin | hidden.
# Unset = public — the network's standing policy is that discovery documents
# stay free; these knobs exist so the 402 experiment can tighten the full
# corpus per-satellite without a redeploy of anything else. The hub's
# page-tier ceilings can also tighten either network-wide (a satellite can
# never loosen below the hub). Inert on older package versions.
# LLMS_SMALL_TIER=public
# LLMS_FULL_TIER=public

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Iconify (dash_emoji_mart.iconify)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the /iconify page caches Iconify API responses (24h TTL). Production
# points at the mounted disk; locally the default temp dir is fine.
# DASH_EMOJI_MART_CACHE_DIR=/var/data/iconify-cache
